#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124757 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d275a218-aa12-54bd-a4ff-4be892226f4f" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a3199e0-7ca6-5317-9afa-2d99c3b3771e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a3199e0-7ca6-5317-9afa-2d99c3b3771e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5+t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357316} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d7476b-5763-583f-adf2-eca36812c205" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121558} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58069a6a-b603-54fd-bc70-e51cd1dd4dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58069a6a-b603-54fd-bc70-e51cd1dd4dd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357317} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed0572da-5a04-5fb8-88a9-093250d4d10a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121559}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ca21829b-f75e-5a9d-97e2-6ce18378c4e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-236986" :question/problem "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-5,7,1)$ and $Q(-4,-1,6).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [$ {{field-2}} $,1]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $7-8t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | $1+5t$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ -8t \\\\ 5t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5+t \\\\ 7-8t \\\\ 1+5t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-5+t \\\\ y=7-8t \\\\ z=1+5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124866 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equations of a Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b80a7c1-1043-53df-9937-1c302aea271a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357326} {:answer/id #uuid "c7131830-fa04-52c9-8165-83976213e7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4+t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=2-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357327} {:answer/id #uuid "26149efd-6258-5c6d-899b-8b76bd92f6a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357328} {:answer/id #uuid "a1bd0392-0d4d-5e20-af94-0f8eea17c8ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=5+t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357329} {:answer/id #uuid "31cb1ef6-a234-5bb7-b23d-06c409656e72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=-t \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2b80a7c1-1043-53df-9937-1c302aea271a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357326} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9a7ef8f-c4b6-5c5b-9714-eade580df09e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b3a37d06-4a0c-5126-bd3b-fbb999a13c7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36026" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1+4t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+2t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+4t \\\\ y=4-t \\\\ z=-2+2t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
